# Requirement formats (ARO and User Story)

Use these formats in milestone and plan **Requirements** sections so technical work and UX stay distinct and scannable.

## ARO (Action, Result, Object)

**Pattern:** three short segments in order: **action** → **result** → **object**.

| Part | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Action** | Verb or short verb phrase: what must be done |
| **Result** | Very short description of the outcome |
| **Object** | Target system, artifact, or place the change applies |

**When to use:** Technical and system requirements where there is **no** clear human persona (infrastructure, schemas, integration, orchestration internals).

**How to write:** Keep each segment to a phrase or single clause. In markdown, label the three parts explicitly, for example:

- **ARO:** **Action:** … **Result:** … **Object:** …

**Examples:**

- **ARO:** **Action:** Update mappings **Result:** to reflect registered tools **Object:** on the orchestration model.
- **ARO:** **Action:** Provision a database **Result:** containing preset seed values **Object:** on application bootstrap.

## User Story

**Pattern:** `As a [persona] I want to [action] so that [outcome]`

| Part | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Persona** | Who interacts with the system (see below) |
| **Action** | Very brief description of what must happen |
| **Outcome** | The benefit the persona gets |

**When to use:** Describing **user experience (UX)** and human goals so requirements stay customer-centric.

**How to write:** One sentence. No extra sub-clauses unless essential.

**Examples:**

- As an **Analyst**, I want to **start a new conversation** so that **I can describe my problem**.
- As an **Admin**, I want to **reset user passwords** so that **I can unblock my team**.

## Personas for user stories

Prefer personas from `.cursor/rules/personas.mdc`: **Analysts**, **Agents**, and **Knowledge Admins** (use the singular form in the sentence: “As an Analyst…”, “As an Agent…”, “As a Knowledge Admin…”).

For **platform or user-management** stories (accounts, enrollment, password lifecycle) where no other persona fits, **Admin** is acceptable.

## Guardrails

- Keep each requirement **short** (one ARO line or one user story per bullet).
- Use **known personas** in user stories; do not invent ad-hoc persona names.
- Do not mix ARO and user story in the same bullet—use separate bullets when both views matter.
